<title>USA: UltraFem starts BufferGel trial.</title>
<headline>UltraFem starts BufferGel trial.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ultrafem Inc said on Tuesday it had started a Phase I study of BufferGel, developed by the company's research and development partner ReProtect LLC.</p>
<p>The study, conducted by HIVNET, a unit of the National Institutes of Health, will test the safety of BufferGel for use as a vaginal microbicide for the prevention of AIDS and other sexually transmitted diseases, the company said.</p>
<p>The study will be conducted with 20 women in Providence, R.I. If successful, HIVNET intends to pursue Phase II efficacy trials, UltraFem said.</p>
</text>
